{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"data\":{\"startAt\":0,\"maxResults\":100,\"total\":11,\"isLast\":true,\"appliedContentFormat\":\"html\",\"comments\":[{\"id\":\"3364773\",\"author\":{\"accountId\":\"61aa32d2ef18ca0071a5abec\",\"displayName\":\"Rajith Suvarna\"},\"body\":\"<p data-local-id=\\\"77bcc054c692\\\">Hello <span data-local-id=\\\"403f635a-146a-464e-a209-1cc94d0001fb\\\" data-type=\\\"mention\\\" data-user-id=\\\"qm:77071153-8149-425d-9cc5-2ef53c35a3bd:6d1c14d4-5252-4432-8d57-2260829c7fa1\\\">@Heaven Poirot</span> ,</p><p data-local-id=\\\"f1e087971a53\\\">Thank you for contacting Appriss Retail Support.</p><p data-local-id=\\\"57233b8494eb\\\">We’ve received your ticket and are routing it to the appropriate team for assistance. The assigned representative will follow up as soon as they’ve had a chance to review.<br><br>Kind Regards, </p><p data-local-id=\\\"c43d5ff1cc06\\\">Appriss Retail Support  </p>\",\"created\":\"2026-09-25T17:33:07.876-0400\",\"updated\":\"2026-09-25T17:33:07.876-0400\",\"updateAuthor\":{\"accountId\":\"61aa32d2ef18ca0071a5abec\",\"displayName\":\"Rajith Suvarna\"},\"jsdPublic\":true},{\"id\":\"3364779\",\"author\":{\"accountId\":\"5f8852df6932330076610600\",\"displayName\":\"Nick Hawkins\"},\"body\":\"<p>🤖 Talos triage · confidence: medium</p><p><strong>Talos can make mistakes. Please check important information.</strong></p><p><strong>Verdict</strong><br>No sign of an application defect — the product only reads and displays the transaction counts that the data-load process records, it does not perform the load itself; no known recurring incident matches this symptom.</p><p><strong>What we checked</strong></p><ul><li><p>This client still runs on the older data warehouse, and the &quot;transactions loaded&quot; figure the platform shows is read straight from a tracking record the data-load process writes — there is no code in the application that loads transactions for this client.</p></li><li><p>The load monitoring configured for this client is built around a once-a-day load with a 6:00am (client time) deadline, so a gap during the afternoon would not raise an automatic alert on its own.</p></li><li><p>The internal status screen caches that figure for about ten minutes, which rules out display lag as an explanation for a gap of an hour.</p></li></ul><p><strong>Next</strong></p><ul><li><p>Pull today&#039;s load-progress record for this client and see whether a load run started and then stalled or errored, or whether nothing new arrived after the 4:36pm ET batch.</p></li><li><p>Confirm with the customer that their systems kept sending transaction files after 4:36pm ET.</p></li></ul>\",\"created\":\"2026-09-25T17:39:28.621-0400\",\"updated\":\"2026-09-25T17:39:28.621-0400\",\"updateAuthor\":{\"accountId\":\"5f8852df6932330076610600\",\"displayName\":\"Nick Hawkins\"},\"jsdPublic\":false},{\"id\":\"3364783\",\"author\":{\"accountId\":\"61aa32d2ef18ca0071a5abec\",\"displayName\":\"Rajith Suvarna\"},\"body\":\"<p data-local-id=\\\"92b33f9bfafb\\\">Hello Team,</p><p data-local-id=\\\"8e5eecd9e597\\\">We can see the pipeline for Winn-Dixie (121_SEG) <a href=\\\"https://dev.azure.com/apprissdevops/DataOps/_build/results?buildId=829444&amp;view=logs&amp;j=f50df833-8049-56a5-1c66-c3e72278a341\\\">#20260925.1</a> appears to be running normally, with an average run time of 16m 50s per run.</p><p data-local-id=\\\"6842df940503\\\">We are receiving *seg_121*pgp* files in the current time frame. Also, files are being processed in the pipeline.</p><figure data-local-id=\\\"934521b5900b\\\" data-type=\\\"media-single\\\" data-layout=\\\"align-start\\\" data-width=\\\"1244\\\" data-width-type=\\\"pixel\\\"><div data-type=\\\"media\\\" data-media-type=\\\"file\\\" data-id=\\\"84d92916-3e9e-49c8-b2cc-1368f132aaf0\\\" data-alt=\\\"image-20260925-214035.png\\\" data-width=\\\"1614\\\" data-height=\\\"568\\\"></div></figure><figure data-local-id=\\\"759043e29e3a\\\" data-type=\\\"media-single\\\" data-layout=\\\"align-start\\\" data-width=\\\"1244\\\" data-width-type=\\\"pixel\\\"><div data-type=\\\"media\\\" data-media-type=\\\"file\\\" data-id=\\\"3b30db3f-5b17-4e8c-9f0c-1da85a1c8091\\\" data-alt=\\\"image-20260925-214056.png\\\" data-width=\\\"1648\\\" data-height=\\\"934\\\"></div></figure><figure data-local-id=\\\"5dc23910abd7\\\" data-type=\\\"media-single\\\" data-layout=\\\"align-start\\\" data-width=\\\"1221\\\" data-width-type=\\\"pixel\\\"><div data-type=\\\"media\\\" data-media-type=\\\"file\\\" data-id=\\\"88cb0ca3-3a2d-401e-a946-54392b1501e1\\\" data-alt=\\\"image-20260925-214122.png\\\" data-width=\\\"1735\\\" data-height=\\\"784\\\"></div></figure><p data-local-id=\\\"f2b42f429ad5\\\">calculating each run as <strong>End Time minus Start Time</strong>. For the first run, I used <code>Running task clean_trickle.py</code> at <strong>08:24:00</strong> as the start event.</p><table data-local-id=\\\"bc5bf25d-4413-4d7d-a8d7-1180add22033\\\"><thead><tr><th data-local-id=\\\"551f4a2c747a\\\" data-colwidth=\\\"96\\\"><p data-local-id=\\\"59d1de74096c\\\">Run</p></th><th data-local-id=\\\"97fb7238380b\\\" data-colwidth=\\\"169\\\"><p data-local-id=\\\"14a2c019810f\\\">Start Time</p></th><th data-local-id=\\\"5fe5929ecde7\\\" data-colwidth=\\\"183\\\"><p data-local-id=\\\"7af278d3accb\\\">End Time</p></th><th data-local-id=\\\"4dffa226d429\\\" data-colwidth=\\\"530\\\"><p data-local-id=\\\"85dff43ee904\\\">Time Taken for each run to Complete</p></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td data-local-id=\\\"123361b77879\\\" data-colwidth=\\\"96\\\"><p data-local-id=\\\"24f45b121abf\\\">1</p></td><td data-local-id=\\\"e56277e7e183\\\" data-colwidth=\\\"169\\\"><p data-local-id=\\\"edec93a1384e\\\">08:24:00</p></td><td data-local-id=\\\"5eeb7f19ffc0\\\" data-colwidth=\\\"183\\\"><p data-local-id=\\\"956c85afadd3\\\">08:39:56</p></td><td data-local-id=\\\"0625567d2d68\\\" data-colwidth=\\\"530\\\"><p data-local-id=\\\"73a182017649\\\"><strong>15m 56s</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td data